{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --local-memory-md /workspace/paper/memory.md --global-memory-md /workspace/investigation/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl /workspace/investigation/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\"step\\\":\\\"verify\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Episode-record audit supports a standalone limitations-first comparison, not a universal improvement or nonlinear-mechanism claim. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=No new scientific experiment or campaign recommendation is introduced.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"All seven summary coverage values, paired width differences and baseline zero-width counts agree with all 256 episode records. Case summaries occur only in episode zero. Candidate has no zero-width intervals; rare-case PPI++ and labeled asymptotic intervals each collapse 115 times, versus two PPI collapses. Available evidence does not identify case generators, sample sizes, named datasets, or measured affine-versus-spline ablations. Metadata reports unverified candidate diagnostics; replay flags are not proofs of statistical validity. No study.* grounding IDs exist, so search score differences and attempt comparisons will not be paper claims.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Write mirrored ready strategy outputs with an early concept figure, direct per-condition coverage/width views, a rare-outcome diagnostic, substantive supplement, and explicit bibliography and reproducibility gaps.\\\"}'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
