{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"apply_patch() {\n  awk '\n    /\"'^'\"\\\\*\\\\*\\\\* Begin Patch\"'$/ { next }\n    /''^'\"\\\\*\\\\*\\\\* Add File: / { if (output \"'!= \"\") close(output); output = substr($0, length(\"*** Add File: \") + 1); next }\n    /''^'\"\\\\*\\\\*\\\\* End Patch\"'$/ { if (output != \"\") close(output); output = \"\"; next }\n    /''^'\"\\\\+/ { if (output == \\\"\\\") exit 2; print substr(\"'$0, 2) > output; next }\n    { exit 3 }\n  '\"'\n}\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Frozen-Score Mean Inference: Width Gains and Coverage Limits\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"With labels, unlabeled scores, and the predictor held fixed within each comparison, what interval-width gains and coverage limitations does honest score calibration exhibit for a binary population mean relative to prediction-powered and labeled-only intervals?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"Across seven evaluated binary-mean conditions, honest score calibration has a small paired width advantage over the evaluated PPI++ comparator in only one condition, while rare-outcome interval collapse exposes why width comparisons must be accompanied by coverage uncertainty and an exact-binomial reference.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation: 256 seeded repetitions, seven conditions, paired interval endpoints, and per-condition coverage and width-difference uncertainty. These support a standalone study of conditional gains, costs, and failure modes, not universal superiority or an identified causal benefit of nonlinear calibration. The primary asymptotic interval and the separately implemented, unmeasured finite-sample safety interval must remain distinct. Cases share one research question and estimator interface; they are not separately named application studies. Final qualification is reported independently of search selection and is not a theorem of nominal coverage.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"recentered\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"Fresh framing, not an edit: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper, aggregated, or extra_tasks directories are present. The enum recentered denotes centering the task's broad opportunity question on the actual condition-specific final evidence, not changing an existing manuscript. A generic improvement story is rejected; a broad cross-method search narrative lacks measured comparisons; the selected standalone story is a coverage-aware width study of the evaluated score-control method.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"No prior manuscript or newly staged edit-mode implementation is available, so preserving, broadening, or replacing a prior title or figure plan is not applicable.\\\",\n+    \\\"The selected candidate source under results/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src identifies the binary superpopulation target, two-fold calibrator, stabilized asymptotic primary interval, and separate safety construction. result.top_program_01 links that candidate path to search selection; the final evidence records a frozen program-tree digest, but no separate final source tree is staged for file-by-file comparison.\\\",\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.final_evaluation independently reports completed and qualified, with 256 episodes. Its case summaries, endpoints, and uncertainty replace the source preparation notes' earlier absence of executed evidence; those notes still correctly distinguish the primary and unmeasured safety tracks.\\\",\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.downstream_study and study.* grounding sources are absent. Do not manufacture an original-incumbent comparison, search improvement, or scored/unscored attempt accounting from memory or aggregate campaign totals.\\\",\n+    \\\"The bibliography is present but central PPI/PPI++, exact-binomial, and empirical-Bernstein sources are missing. Existing DML and GCV metadata are relevant leads, not proof of having read those works. Off-topic retrieval records do not enlarge the study's scientific scope.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Honest frozen-score controls\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The studied estimator fits clipped ridge affine/spline score transforms on complementary labeled folds, uses rho=N/(n+N), and returns a Wilson-style stabilized asymptotic Wald interval, with a sample-size-only exact-binomial branch below 16 labels. This is the evaluated primary method, not a universally finite-sample-valid procedure.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Evaluated PPI++ mean interval\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Primary efficiency comparator with paired endpoints and uncertainty in all seven conditions; identifies the single small width reduction and six width increases. Describe the evaluated comparator, not all possible PPI++ implementations.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Evaluated PPI mean interval\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Original prediction-powered reference has measured endpoints and reveals different width/coverage behavior from PPI++, especially in the rare-outcome condition. Include in the compact main results table and rare-outcome figure, with complete comparisons in the supplement.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Labeled-only asymptotic mean interval\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Separates benefits over label-only normal inference from benefits over prediction-powered inference; its rare-outcome collapse is measured rather than an untested failure hypothesis.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Labeled-only exact binomial interval\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Provides a finite-sample coverage reference under independent Bernoulli sampling. Its conservatism and width are essential context, not a matched-validity justification for the asymptotic primary method.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Bounded componentwise safety construction\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Source implements separate empirical-Bernstein residual/control bounds and fixed-weight aggregation. Explain assumptions and union-bound logic as a theoretical alternative, never as an evaluated series or a reason to label the returned interval exact.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Use final.evidence.episodes as the numerical source, especially episodes[0].solution.case_summaries and all episodes[*].solution.cases. Summary coverage, paired mean differences, and zero-width counts were checked against the 256 records for each case. Retain neutral labels C1-C7 because generators, named datasets, and case-specific sample sizes are not identified in these records.\\\",\n+    \\\"Primary paired comparison: candidate-minus-PPI++ mean width difference is -0.00030173260155952255 in C2, with reported 95% interval [-0.0004003584986521721, -0.000203106704466873]. The other six differences are positive. These are condition-specific width findings, not a multiplicity-adjusted universal conclusion or a causal spline ablation.\\\",\n+    \\\"Display per-condition empirical coverage with reported uncertainty alongside width differences. Candidate coverage ranges from 0.9296875 to 0.95703125, and all seven reported candidate coverage intervals include 0.95. Non-rejection is not evidence that nominal coverage has been established.\\\",\n+    \\\"C5 is explicitly the low-mean condition: recorded truth 0.006800000000000005. Evaluated PPI++ and labeled-only asymptotic coverage are 0.55078125, each with 115 zero-width intervals. Candidate coverage is 0.9296875 with no zero-width intervals; exact-binomial coverage is 0.99609375. The candidate-minus-exact width difference is -0.000046988429386779555 with interval [-0.00032065914173324357, 0.0002266822829596845], so this comparison is inconclusive on mean width.\\\",\n+    \\\"Explain the observed label-only width reductions in C1-C3 and the small widening relative to labeled-only asymptotic intervals in C4, C6, and C7. Put PPI, PPI++, both labeled-only references, and candidate on a single compact comparison table, split into readable blocks if necessary.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final aggregate coverage 0.9425223214285714 and mean width 0.12988779848794016 are descriptive summaries, not evidence of exact 95% validity. Do not calculate a binomial uncertainty interval by treating all seven within-seed conditions as independent repetitions.\\\",\n+    \\\"Do not lead with the aggregate width ratio 64175.10539621905. Near-zero and zero comparator widths make ratio summaries misleading; emphasize raw paired width differences, interval distributions, coverage, and collapse counts instead. Do not infer the evaluator's ratio regularization formula.\\\",\n+    \\\"No measured affine-versus-spline ablation, safety-track width, oracle attainment, named real-data result, or matched comparison to the original search incumbent exists in the supplied paper evidence. Do not fill these gaps with unscored methods or source-only functions.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"An early full-text-width conceptual overview shows immutable labels/scores, complementary-fold score calibration, residual correction, the evaluated asymptotic interval, and a visually separate unmeasured safety construction.\\\",\n+    \\\"A full-text-width four-panel comparison pairs empirical coverage with candidate-minus-baseline width differences for C1-C4 and C5-C7; show the nominal coverage line and zero-difference line, with pointwise uncertainty and fixed method colors.\\\",\n+    \\\"A full-text-width two-panel rare-outcome diagnostic presents empirical interval-width distributions and zero-width counts in C5, making collapsed intervals visible instead of rewarding them through ratios.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"frozen_score_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the estimand, immutable-input restriction, fold isolation, and distinction between evaluated primary and unmeasured safety intervals immediately legible.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"information_flow\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none_conceptual\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"evaluated_primary_vs_unmeasured_safety\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected ICLR article style is single-column with a 5.5-inch text width and 9-inch text height. Use all 5.5 inches for a shallow five-object diagram; a half-text-width placement would crowd the fold-isolation labels. Place on page 1 or 2, preferably page 2 near the problem definition.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 5,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Five grouped objects: immutable labeled/unlabeled score inputs; complementary-fold fit/evaluate pairing; finite-N residual correction for E[Y]; evaluated stabilized asymptotic interval with size-only exact fallback; separate unmeasured bounded safety interval. Use solid primary and dashed safety connectors. No extra labels, predictor retraining, chronological arrows, or empirical-gain badge.\\\",\n+      \\\"target_size_inches\\\": [5.5, 1.8],\n+      \\\"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"intended_paper_footprint\\\": \\\"About one quarter page including caption, inside the formulation allocation.\\\",\n+      \\\"export_contract\\\": \\\"Retain editable draw.io source and prompt log; export vector PDF when available plus PNG at 300 DPI. Use PDF in LaTeX whenever present. If genuinely raster-only, regenerate at least 2400 pixels wide rather than upscaling.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"coverage_width_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Show that the small isolated PPI++ width gain and other width increases must be assessed jointly with empirical coverage and its uncertainty.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"paired_forest_composite\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"evaluation_condition\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"empirical_coverage_and_paired_mean_width_difference\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"C1-C4_then_C5-C7_with_coverage_and_width_columns\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Use a 5.5-inch-wide, 2-by-2 grid in the inspected single-column style: coverage left, width difference right, C1-C4 above C5-C7. This keeps at most four conditions in any panel without shrinking seven long case labels or five method series into half a text column. Subpanels are approximately 2.4 inches wide and use concise labels and shared legends.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Coverage panels: candidate, evaluated PPI++, labeled-only asymptotic, and exact binomial, with the reported 95% coverage intervals and a 0.95 reference. Width panels: paired candidate-minus-PPI++, candidate-minus-labeled-asymptotic, and candidate-minus-exact differences with reported 95% intervals and a zero line. Negative means narrower, not necessarily valid or superior. Preserve all seven conditions in fixed numeric order; group them only to satisfy readability. Width panels may use separately labeled linear scales because C5's difference is much larger. State pointwise rather than simultaneous uncertainty. PPI comparisons remain in the table and rare-outcome figure.\\\",\n+      \\\"target_size_inches\\\": [5.5, 4.3],\n+      \\\"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 8.5,\n+      \\\"intended_paper_footprint\\\": \\\"About three fifths of a page including caption, inside the main comparison allocation.\\\",\n+      \\\"export_contract\\\": \\\"Generate both PDF and PNG from plotting source, with PNG at 300 DPI; reference the PDF from LaTeX. Never recover legibility by raster upscaling.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"rare_outcome_diagnostic\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Expose degenerate comparator intervals and the inconclusive width comparison with exact-binomial inference in the observed low-mean condition.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"ecdf_and_zero_width_counts\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"interval_method\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"interval_width_distribution_and_zero_width_count\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"C5_only\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Two side-by-side quantitative panels need the complete 5.5-inch single-column text width for readable ECDF axes, zero-width annotations, and four method labels. A half-width figure would make each panel too narrow. Use a shared four-method legend and label counts rather than a thresholded success metric.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Use candidate, evaluated PPI++, evaluated PPI, and exact binomial. Plot empirical width CDFs from the 256 C5 endpoint records, retaining the mass at zero on a linear axis; show the corresponding zero-width counts in panel two. Mention that the labeled-only asymptotic comparator also has 115 zero-width intervals in the caption and main table. Pair the figure with coverage values and intervals in the main text, not only in the supplement. Do not claim the zero-width diagnostic proves the internal cause of every miss.\\\",\n+      \\\"target_size_inches\\\": [5.5, 2.2],\n+      \\\"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 8.5,\n+      \\\"intended_paper_footprint\\\": \\\"About one third page including caption, inside the failure-analysis allocation.\\\",\n+      \\\"export_contract\\\": \\\"Generate PDF and 300-DPI PNG from the same plotting source and reference the PDF. Any unavoidable raster-only full-width replacement must be regenerated at least 2400 pixels wide.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Provide the source-level implementation detail, complete measured comparator evidence, and reproducibility boundaries needed to audit the standalone claim without moving its isolated gain, widening, low-mean failures, or coverage caveats out of the main paper.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete paired interval comparisons\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tables for all seven conditions and all measured baseline intervals: empirical coverage and its reported limits, paired mean width differences and limits, recorded ratio diagnostics clearly distinguished from ratio-of-means, and zero-width counts. Derive tabulations only from final episode records; mark any derived summary and record its formula. Do not copy the first episode's aggregate case summaries 256 times.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Calibration and interval implementation\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Source-grounded pseudocode for fold generation, training-only quantile knots, ridge/GCV selection, clipping, rho weighting, pooled variance approximation, boundary stabilization, and the size-only exact fallback. Describe affine-only and safety functions as available but unmeasured. Cite result.top_program_01 as the path link, not as numerical evidence of these implementation properties; use the linked program.py and METHOD.md directly.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Fixed-control variance and separate safety argument\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Check the source's fixed-control variance decomposition, conditional-mean oracle expression, and affine projection gap under iid common-population sampling and an independently frozen predictor. Extend with the componentwise empirical-Bernstein union-bound argument under bounded residuals and controls, explaining cross-fold dependence and fixed nonnegative weights. Label these as mathematical arguments, not measured oracle attainment or a guarantee for the returned asymptotic interval.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Evidence extraction and reproducibility boundaries\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document final evidence paths and hashes, the 256 episode seeds, case identifiers, recorded truths, paired endpoint extraction, and scripts mapping every proposed table/plot to records. Preserve the final qualification and the unverified diagnostic-trust annotation. Explain that the supplied study helpers are not an executed end-to-end experiment runner, and that case generators, case-specific n/N values, and a separately staged final source tree are not recoverable here; reproducing figures from records is narrower than reproducing data generation.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\", \\\"result.top_program_01\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the documented agent-assisted ideation, candidate preparation, reference planning, and paper framing/writing roles using the visible task and source-preparation records; distinguish automated evaluation from author-generated numerical evidence. Do not invent model identifiers, manual verification, or unlogged human contributions. Final episode records provide the provenance anchor for measured results, not a claim that LLMs verified statistical validity.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Phases\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Valid Result\\\",\n+    \\\"Iteration History\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Winning Program\\\",\n+    \\\"Universal Improvements\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"uniformly narrower valid intervals\\\",\n+    \\\"95% coverage is established because it was not rejected\\\",\n+    \\\"cross-fitting guarantees finite-sample validity\\\",\n+    \\\"the spline component caused the gain\\\",\n+    \\\"unscored attempts were measured losses\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"Scope: this is a standalone empirical/methodological limitations study, not a search diary, architecture contribution, or new universally valid CI procedure. Neutral cases are separate evidence blocks under one common binary-mean question; do not name a dataset from the task's optional menu or infer case mechanisms from observed gains.\\\",\n+    \\\"Qualification audit, private provenance: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, final.qualification.correct=true. No failed final qualification is reported in this run. Do not overwrite these with search flags or imply that qualification proves scientific validity. Gate-specific diagnostics beyond the supplied fields are unknown. If later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, preserve that outcome and limitations in the paper, review, audit, and revisions without guessing whether the cause is performance, validity, or adaptivity.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private provenance only: use result.top_program_01 to locate the selected source. With no downstream_study or study.* sources, omit search-score deltas, scored/unscored attempt counts, and original-incumbent superiority claims. Internal pipeline labels and source paths belong in private grounding or anonymized reproducibility records, not reader-facing titles or claims.\\\",\n+    \\\"Target discipline: E[Y] is the binary superpopulation mean. Inputs are fixed across methods within a repetition; uncertainty is assessed over repeated draws, not by silently changing the target to the realized finite-pool mean. Common-population iid sampling and predictor independence are assumptions, not properties established for unidentified generators. The finite-N oracle formulas and fold-variance approximation must be distinguished.\\\",\n+    \\\"Theory can explain the opportunity, not attribute the measured effect: for a fixed control, state the variance decomposition and conditional-mean optimum under explicit assumptions; the estimated clipped spline family need not attain the oracle. Include no nonlinear-versus-affine efficacy claim without measured matched ablation. Treat the safety construction as separate and unmeasured throughout captions, abstract, review, and conclusions.\\\",\n+    \\\"Uncertainty: retain the supplied per-condition coverage intervals and paired width-difference intervals, label them pointwise, and state that seven conditions and multiple baselines were examined. Existing non-rejection flags are not equivalence tests or guarantees. Describe seeds as seeded repetitions; independence of all within-seed conditions is not established. Endpoint replay flags and unverified candidate diagnostics do not certify statistical coverage.\\\",\n+    \\\"Venue/layout: read VENUE.md and the inspected templates/iclr/paper.tex plus paper.sty; the practical geometry is one 5.5-inch text column by 9 inches. All three required figures use the full text width, not a nonexistent two-column figure* geometry. Target readable final labels of at least 8.5 points for plots and 9 points for the overview. Keep diagrams shallow and use a 2-by-2 grid rather than seven-category crowded panels.\\\",\n+    \\\"Body budget: target 8.5 pages excluding references: abstract/introduction and concrete contributions 1.25; formulation/related work plus early overview 1.25; method and limited theoretical analysis 2.0; evaluation design and provenance limits 1.0; direct coverage/width comparison including compact table 1.75; rare-outcome analysis 0.75; limitations/conclusion 0.5. These allocations sum to 8.5 and include figures. Use available space for estimand clarity, fold isolation, comparator coverage, and failure analysis rather than more unsupported experiments. Final body must be 8-9 pages; if exactly 8 pages, the last must be at least 75% occupied. This is a plan, not a measured pagination result.\\\",\n+    \\\"Suggested thesis-first sections: Introduction; Problem and Related Work; Honest Frozen-Score Controls; Evaluation Design; Coverage and Width Across Conditions; Rare-Outcome Limits; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Explain the missing nonlinear ablation, absent safety measurement, unidentified generators/sample sizes, narrow binary target, and no distribution-shift or new-domain validation explicitly. No padding or chronological branch descriptions.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main evidence table: include all five evaluated inferential methods; omit the [0,1] sanity interval from headline efficiency comparisons. Use compact condition labels and split coverage/width blocks if needed. Keep the one C2 improvement, six PPI++ widenings, C5 collapse counts, and candidate coverage caveat in the main body. Do not infer evaluator internals from field names such as valid_gain_supported.\\\",\n+    \\\"Supplement: after the references use clearpage, appendix, and a substantive Supplementary Information section with the planned subsections. Route later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses there without changing this strategy. Keep evidence essential to the central thesis in the main text. Include the separate LLM Usage disclosure required by the venue.\\\",\n+    \\\"Template repair for later drafting: the staged ICLR scaffold contains a named author and iclrfinalcopy, so use anonymous review mode and remove author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, and identifying links. Preserve any orchestrator-owned watermark block. The staged style provides practical geometry but does not itself establish official ICLR 2026 template provenance; verify the required venue version through permitted official material before final submission.\\\",\n+    \\\"Literature limitation: references.bib/references_provenance.json presently supply DML and GCV metadata but omit the central permitted PPI/PPI++ starter works and exact-binomial/empirical-Bernstein foundations. Before a final manuscript, obtain and actually consult exact allowlisted starter/foundational sources; verify bibliographic metadata, including GCV's venue field. Do not invent missing citation keys or cite unrelated retrieval hits as padding. Never search citation networks, guess the prohibited paper, or inspect ambiguous follow-up material. This strategy stage performs no literature retrieval and makes no claim that metadata equals source consultation.\\\",\n+    \\\"Vector-first delivery: quantitative plotting scripts must emit PDF and PNG at 300 DPI, and LaTeX must reference PDF whenever available. Preserve editable concept-figure output and follow the orchestrator's generate-concept-figure handoff later, not during strategy generation. Raster-only replacements require regeneration at least 2400 pixels wide full-width or 1200 pixels wide column-width; never upscale. Keep method colors and validity labels consistent across figures.\\\",\n+    \\\"Evidence gaps are limitations, not promised experiments. Available endpoints suffice for the planned comparisons and CDFs; no new data collection, predictor retraining, safety-track rerun, or later ablation is necessary to make the narrow thesis readable. Do not report these missing studies as completed. Reproduction of the sealed data-generating experiment remains incomplete even if every table can be regenerated from the released records.\\\",\n+    \\\"Planning stage only: write neither paper.tex nor claims_grounding.json, generate no figures, and do not run final-paper validation. Validate only this strategy's JSON structure, source references, consistency, and output boundaries.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Strategy: Frozen-Score Mean Inference\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Status:** ready. **Family:** \"'`paper_standalone`, compatible with `write-paper-standalone`.\n+\n+**Provisional title:** *Frozen-Score Mean Inference: Width Gains and Coverage Limits*.\n+\n+**Central question:** With labels, unlabeled scores, and the predictor fixed within each comparison, what interval-width gains and coverage limitations does honest score calibration exhibit for a binary population mean relative to prediction-powered and labeled-only intervals?\n+\n+**Central thesis:** Across seven evaluated binary-mean conditions, honest score calibration has a small paired width advantage over the evaluated PPI++ comparator in only one condition; rare-outcome interval collapse shows why widths need coverage uncertainty and an exact-binomial reference alongside them.\n+\n+This is a standalone empirical/methodological limitations paper, not a claim of universal improvement or a demonstration that nonlinear calibration caused the observed gain. The shared object is binary superpopulation-mean inference from immutable inputs. Present neutral conditions C1-C7 as evidence blocks under that question, not as named application studies or chronological experiments.\n+\n+## Evidence and Qualification\n+\n+Read `paper_data.json.final_evaluation` independently. It reports a completed, qualified final evaluation. The authoritative qualification anchors are `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, and `final.qualification.correct`; no failed final qualification is reported here. This status is not a guarantee of nominal statistical coverage. Missing gate-specific diagnostics remain unknown, and neither replay flags nor unverified candidate diagnostics prove statistical validity. If later authoritative evidence changes qualification, preserve the reported outcome and limitations through writing, review, audit, and revision without guessing the cause.\n+\n+The numerical anchor is `final.evidence.episodes`: 256 seeded repetitions, each containing seven conditions and paired candidate/baseline intervals. The aggregate case summaries occur only at `episodes[0].solution.case_summaries`; individual records are under `episodes[*].solution.cases`. All seven coverage summaries, paired mean width differences, and baseline zero-width counts were checked against those records. The diagnostic-trust annotation is `unverified`; the plan relies on recorded endpoints, truths, and comparisons, not on candidate-supplied validity assertions.\n+\n+The final aggregate coverage is **0.9425223214285714** and mean width **0.12988779848794016** (`final.metric.coverage`, `final.metric.mean_width`). These are descriptive, not proof of 95% validity. Do not treat all seven within-seed cases as independent when constructing aggregate uncertainty. Per-condition candidate coverage ranges from **0.9296875** to **0.95703125**; every reported candidate coverage interval includes 0.95. Non-rejection is not equivalence or validation of nominal coverage.\n+\n+`downstream_study` and `study.*` grounding sources are absent. Omit search-score deltas, scored/unscored attempt accounting, and superiority to an original search incumbent. Missing evaluations are not measured losses. The measured PPI++ comparator is not automatically the original search incumbent. Internal selection metadata is private provenance, not a visible paper result.\n+\n+## Framing Alternatives and Edit Decision\n+\n+No resolved edit-context files, `previous_paper/`, `aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` are staged. This is fresh framing, not an update to a prior manuscript. The JSON enum is **recentered** only to describe recentering the broad task opportunity around the actual final evidence; it does not assert a prior paper existed.\n+\n+- **Preserve a generic improvement story:** reject. Only one condition is narrower than evaluated PPI++; finite-sample validity of the returned method is not established.\n+- **Broaden to a shared family of searched methods:** reject. Other branches do not supply the necessary measured comparisons; source-only functions and unsuccessful executions are not performance evidence.\n+- **Center the evaluated score-control method'\"'s width/coverage limits:** select. It has repeated paired measurements, uncertainty, a small isolated gain, widespread modest costs, and an informative low-mean failure comparison.\n+\n+The selected candidate source is under \"'`results/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/`, linked by `result.top_program_01`. Inspect `program.py`, `METHOD.md`, and `study.py` directly for implementation facts. The final evidence records a frozen program-tree digest, but a separate final source tree is not staged for file-by-file comparison. The candidate'\"'s preparation notes predate execution; final episode records supersede their absence-of-results statements, not their warnings about asymptotic versus safety intervals.\n+\n+## Method Groups\n+\n+1. **Honest frozen-score controls — proposed.** Two-fold complementary-label calibration; ridge affine and small piecewise-linear spline candidates selected by training-only GCV; clipped controls; finite-unlabeled-sample factor \"'`rho=N/(n+N)`; residual correction. The evaluated output is a Wilson-style stabilized asymptotic Wald interval, with a size-only Clopper-Pearson branch for fewer than 16 labels. Do not call the general procedure exact or an exact Wilson interval.\n+2. **Evaluated PPI++ mean interval — primary baseline.** The paired efficiency comparison is central. Restrict claims to this evaluated comparator rather than all implementations of the published method.\n+3. **Evaluated PPI mean interval — baseline.** Retain in the main table, rare-outcome plot, and complete supplement. Its behavior differs materially from PPI++.\n+4. **Labeled-only asymptotic mean interval — baseline.** Separates gains over label-only normal inference from gains over prediction-powered inference.\n+5. **Labeled-only exact binomial interval — baseline.** Finite-sample reference under iid Bernoulli sampling, not permission to transfer its guarantee to another estimator.\n+6. **Bounded componentwise safety construction — supporting theory only.** The source implements empirical-Bernstein component intervals and union-bound/fixed-weight aggregation separately. It was not the measured primary output; do not assign it empirical coverage or width.\n+\n+Exclude partition portfolios and likelihood branches from the main comparison. An affine-only matched calibration function exists but has no measured ablation in the supplied evidence. Likewise, the oracle frontier and safety helper are not executed evidence of superiority.\n+\n+Keep the target **E[Y]**, not the realized finite-pool mean. Inputs are fixed across methods within each repetition; frequentist uncertainty is over repeated draws. Common-population iid sampling and a predictor frozen independently of inference labels are assumptions, not established facts about unidentified generators. Explain the fixed-control variance decomposition, conditional-mean oracle, affine projection gap, and fold-variance approximation with their separate assumptions. A fixed clipped spline dictionary need not attain the oracle; cross-fitting does not make folds unconditionally independent.\n+\n+## Results That Carry the Story\n+\n+Use `final.evidence.episodes` for this entire section. Retain C1-C7 identifiers: the records do not identify datasets, generators, or case-specific sample sizes. Do not infer a nonlinear, shifted, or adversarial regime from a result pattern.\n+\n+- **One small PPI++ width gain:** in C2, candidate-minus-PPI++ mean width difference is **-0.00030173260155952255**, with reported 95% interval **[-0.0004003584986521721, -0.000203106704466873]**. The other six differences are positive. These are pointwise, condition-specific findings, not multiplicity-adjusted general improvement or evidence attributing the effect to splines.\n+- **Label-only context:** C1-C3 are narrower than labeled-only asymptotic inference; C4, C6, and C7 have small width increases against that baseline. Report the exact-binomial and PPI comparisons too, rather than selecting only favorable baselines.\n+- **Rare-outcome diagnostic:** C5 records truth **0.006800000000000005**. PPI++ and labeled-only asymptotic coverage are each **0.55078125**, with **115** zero-width intervals each. Candidate coverage is **0.9296875**, with no zero-width intervals; exact-binomial coverage is **0.99609375**. PPI has two zero-width intervals. Collapse and undercoverage are observable; the evaluator'\"'s internal cause for every miss is not identified.\n+- **Exact reference remains important:** in C5, candidate-minus-exact mean width difference is **-0.000046988429386779555**, with interval **[-0.00032065914173324357, 0.0002266822829596845]**. This width comparison is inconclusive. The candidate's absence of collapsed intervals does not establish nominal validity or superiority to exact inference.\n+- **Avoid unstable ratio headlines:** the retained aggregate width ratio is **64175.10539621905**. Zero and near-zero comparator widths make ratio summaries scientifically misleading; foreground paired differences and raw width distributions. Do not infer the evaluator's denominator regularization.\n+\n+The main table must include all five evaluated inferential methods. Split coverage and width blocks if necessary. Keep the C2 gain, six PPI++ widenings, C5 collapse counts, and candidate coverage caveat in the main body. The \"'`[0,1]` sanity interval is not a headline efficiency baseline. Do not translate evaluator flags into scientific validity claims.\n+\n+## Figures and Practical Geometry\n+\n+Inspected `paper.sty` and `.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex`. The style has **one 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height**. There is no two-column body: all required figures use full text width, not `figure*` to span nonexistent columns. The scaffold'\"'s author and final-copy mode must be replaced for anonymous review during later drafting. Practical geometry does not certify the official 2026 template version; verify that provenance before submission.\n+\n+### Figure 1 — \"'`frozen_score_overview`\n+\n+Required early conceptual diagram; generator **`generate-concept-figure`**. Place on page 1 or 2, preferably page 2 beside the problem definition. Target **5.5 × 1.8 inches**, full text width, approximately one quarter page including caption. Five grouped objects show immutable inputs, complementary-fold fitting/evaluation, residual correction targeting E[Y], the evaluated stabilized primary interval, and a separate unmeasured safety construction. Use solid versus dashed connectors for evaluated versus theoretical paths, not chronological discovery arrows. No predictor retraining or empirical-gain badge.\n+\n+Readability budget: **one panel, one panel per row, at most five object groups, three semantic series, labels at least 9 points**. Half-width would crowd fold isolation and track distinctions. Grounding: `result.top_program_01` for the source path, `final.evidence.episodes` for which primary output was measured. Retain editable draw.io output and prompt log; no figure generation occurs in this stage.\n+\n+### Figure 2 — `coverage_width_comparison`\n+\n+Required matplotlib composite; target **5.5 × 4.3 inches**, full text width, approximately three fifths page including caption. Use a **2 × 2 grid**: coverage left, paired width differences right; C1-C4 in the upper row, C5-C7 below. Keep fixed case order, not performance ranking. Each panel has at most four conditions, so seven cases do not crowd one axis.\n+\n+Coverage series: candidate, evaluated PPI++, labeled-only asymptotic, exact binomial. Show the reported coverage uncertainty and 0.95 reference. Difference series: candidate minus PPI++, labeled-only asymptotic, and exact; show reported uncertainty and zero reference. Negative means narrower, not automatically valid. PPI remains in the main table and rare-case figure. Clearly labeled different linear scales are permissible across width panels because C5 is much larger.\n+\n+Readability budget: **four panels, two per row, four categories per panel, four series maximum; final labels at least 8.5 points**. Approximately 2.4-inch subpanels, concise case labels, and shared legends make this possible without shrinking. Grounding: `final.evidence.episodes`, particularly the single attached set of case summaries. Explain that the uncertainty is pointwise, not simultaneous.\n+\n+### Figure 3 — `rare_outcome_diagnostic`\n+\n+Required matplotlib diagnostic; target **5.5 × 2.2 inches**, full text width, approximately one third page including caption. Two side-by-side panels show C5 empirical interval-width CDFs and zero-width counts for candidate, evaluated PPI++, evaluated PPI, and exact binomial. Retain the mass at zero on a linear width axis. Mention the labeled-only asymptotic baseline'\"'s matching 115 collapses in the caption and main table. Put coverage and its uncertainty in adjacent main text, not only the supplement.\n+\n+Readability budget: **two panels, two per row, four method categories, four series; final labels at least 8.5 points**. Full width gives each panel enough room for axes and method labels. Grounding: all 256 C5 endpoint records in \"'`final.evidence.episodes`. Do not imply the collapse diagnostic establishes the internal cause of every coverage miss.\n+\n+### Export Contract\n+\n+Quantitative plotting source emits **PDF and 300-DPI PNG**, and LaTeX references the PDF whenever available. Preserve editable concept output and export PDF when possible. For truly raster-only figures, regenerate at **at least 2400 pixels wide full-width or 1200 pixels wide column-width**; never upscale an existing raster. Use consistent method colors and validity labels. Exactly one overview uses `generate-concept-figure`; follow its later orchestration handoff rather than rendering it during strategy generation.\n+\n+## Body Budget and Organization\n+\n+Target **8.5 pages excluding references**, with figure footprints included:\n+\n+| Scientific content | Planned pages |\n+| --- | ---: |\n+| Abstract, introduction, concrete contributions | 1.25 |\n+| Problem and related work, including early overview | 1.25 |\n+| Honest controls and limited theoretical analysis | 2.00 |\n+| Evaluation design and provenance limitations | 1.00 |\n+| Direct coverage/width comparison and compact table | 1.75 |\n+| Rare-outcome analysis | 0.75 |\n+| Limitations and conclusion | 0.50 |\n+\n+Suggested thesis-first headings: **Introduction; Problem and Related Work; Honest Frozen-Score Controls; Evaluation Design; Coverage and Width Across Conditions; Rare-Outcome Limits; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion**. Additional space buys precise estimands, fold isolation, calibration/stabilization detail, comparator uncertainty, and a checked variance argument—not new experiments or a history of discarded approaches.\n+\n+The venue requires 8-9 body pages; if exactly eight pages, the final page must be at least 75% occupied. These are planned allocations, not a claim that pagination has been validated. Do not pad to meet them. Explicitly retain missing nonlinear ablation, unmeasured safety intervals, unidentified generators/sample sizes, narrow binary scope, no distribution-shift validation, and incomplete end-to-end reproduction.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information\n+\n+After references use a page break, appendix mode, and **Supplementary Information**. Its purpose is audit depth and substantive methods, not hiding central limitations. The following mirrored JSON entries are grounded in existing artifacts:\n+\n+1. **Complete paired interval comparisons** (`final.evidence.episodes`). All seven conditions and all recorded comparators, coverage limits, paired width differences and limits, ratio diagnostics distinguished from ratio-of-means, and zero-width counts. Document formulas for derived tables. Never duplicate the first episode'\"'s aggregate summaries across repetitions.\n+2. **Calibration and interval implementation** (\"'`result.top_program_01`, a path anchor). Use the linked `program.py` and `METHOD.md` for fold generation, train-only knots, ridge/GCV, clipping, rho weighting, approximate variance, stabilization, and the size-only exact fallback. Affine-only and safety functions are available but unmeasured; the scalar selection score does not substantiate implementation properties.\n+3. **Fixed-control variance and separate safety argument** (`result.top_program_01`, linked method sources). Check the decomposition, conditional-mean oracle, and affine projection gap under explicit assumptions. Explain componentwise bounded concentration, union bounds, fold dependence, and nonnegative endpoint weights. This is not observed oracle attainment or validity of the returned asymptotic interval.\n+4. **Evidence extraction and reproducibility boundaries** (`final.evidence.episodes`, `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.correct`, `result.top_program_01`). Record hashes, seeds, truths, endpoint extraction, and table/figure scripts. Retain qualification and diagnostic-trust annotations. Recreating figures from records is possible; case generators, case-specific n/N values, and a separately staged final source tree are not recoverable here. Study helpers are not an executed complete experiment runner.\n+5. **LLM Usage** (`result.top_program_01`, `final.evidence.episodes`, with role descriptions from visible task/source-preparation records). Disclose agent-assisted ideation, implementation preparation, reference planning, and framing/writing accurately; distinguish those roles from automated evaluation. Do not invent model identifiers, human checks, or claims of LLM-verified coverage.\n+\n+Later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses go here without retroactively altering this plan. Never move the isolated gain, widening, rare-outcome failures, or nominal-coverage caveat out of the main paper.\n+\n+## Literature, Anonymity, and Handoff\n+\n+`references.bib` and `references_provenance.json` exist, but central permitted PPI/PPI++ starter sources and exact-binomial/empirical-Bernstein foundations are missing. DML and GCV metadata are relevant leads, not proof of source consultation; GCV'\"'s venue field needs checking. Before final writing, consult exact allowlisted starter/foundational works and verify citation metadata. Do not invent keys or pad related work with off-topic retrieval hits. Do not guess or search for the prohibited paper, traverse citation networks, or inspect ambiguous follow-up material. This framing stage performs no retrieval and does not claim that metadata is reading.\n+\n+The venue is **ICLR 2026, anonymous conference review**. Remove names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, identifying links, and final-copy mode from the seeded scaffold later; preserve the orchestrator-owned watermark block. Include the separate LLM Usage disclosure. Do not falsely certify the old-looking staged style as the official current venue release.\n+\n+This stage writes no \"'`paper.tex`, no `claims_grounding.json`, and no figures, and runs no final-paper validation. Check only strategy structure, source references, consistency, and stage boundaries. Missing experiments remain missing, not promises converted into completed work.\n+\n+## Diary and Overclaim Guardrails\n+\n+Forbid headings centered on **Search Progression, Campaign Phases, Milestones, First Valid Result, Iteration History, Experiment A / Experiment B, Winning Program, Universal Improvements**.\n+\n+Forbid visible phrases **we then tried; subsequent improvements; next-best; later variants; first valid result; correctness rate; correct and eligible; eligible; combined_score; rubric; worker_01; worker_02; uniformly narrower valid intervals; 95% coverage is established because it was not rejected; cross-fitting guarantees finite-sample validity; the spline component caused the gain; unscored attempts were measured losses; state of the art**. Internal selection identifiers in this memo are private provenance only, never recommended reader-facing language.\n+\n+The framing wins because it uses the strongest paired final evidence, preserves unfavorable comparisons, and identifies a useful limitation without inventing a mechanism, a dataset, a universal winner, or an exact guarantee. No failure reason applies to this bounded strategy; bibliography and reproduction gaps remain explicit final-manuscript limitations or remediation requirements.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"apply_patch() {\n  awk '\n    /\"'^'\"\\\\*\\\\*\\\\* Begin Patch\"'$/ { next }\n    /''^'\"\\\\*\\\\*\\\\* Add File: / { if (output \"'!= \"\") close(output); output = substr($0, length(\"*** Add File: \") + 1); next }\n    /''^'\"\\\\*\\\\*\\\\* End Patch\"'$/ { if (output != \"\") close(output); output = \"\"; next }\n    /''^'\"\\\\+/ { if (output == \\\"\\\") exit 2; print substr(\"'$0, 2) > output; next }\n    { exit 3 }\n  '\"'\n}\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Frozen-Score Mean Inference: Width Gains and Coverage Limits\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"With labels, unlabeled scores, and the predictor held fixed within each comparison, what interval-width gains and coverage limitations does honest score calibration exhibit for a binary population mean relative to prediction-powered and labeled-only intervals?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"Across seven evaluated binary-mean conditions, honest score calibration has a small paired width advantage over the evaluated PPI++ comparator in only one condition, while rare-outcome interval collapse exposes why width comparisons must be accompanied by coverage uncertainty and an exact-binomial reference.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation: 256 seeded repetitions, seven conditions, paired interval endpoints, and per-condition coverage and width-difference uncertainty. These support a standalone study of conditional gains, costs, and failure modes, not universal superiority or an identified causal benefit of nonlinear calibration. The primary asymptotic interval and the separately implemented, unmeasured finite-sample safety interval must remain distinct. Cases share one research question and estimator interface; they are not separately named application studies. Final qualification is reported independently of search selection and is not a theorem of nominal coverage.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"recentered\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"Fresh framing, not an edit: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper, aggregated, or extra_tasks directories are present. The enum recentered denotes centering the task's broad opportunity question on the actual condition-specific final evidence, not changing an existing manuscript. A generic improvement story is rejected; a broad cross-method search narrative lacks measured comparisons; the selected standalone story is a coverage-aware width study of the evaluated score-control method.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"No prior manuscript or newly staged edit-mode implementation is available, so preserving, broadening, or replacing a prior title or figure plan is not applicable.\\\",\n+    \\\"The selected candidate source under results/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src identifies the binary superpopulation target, two-fold calibrator, stabilized asymptotic primary interval, and separate safety construction. result.top_program_01 links that candidate path to search selection; the final evidence records a frozen program-tree digest, but no separate final source tree is staged for file-by-file comparison.\\\",\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.final_evaluation independently reports completed and qualified, with 256 episodes. Its case summaries, endpoints, and uncertainty replace the source preparation notes' earlier absence of executed evidence; those notes still correctly distinguish the primary and unmeasured safety tracks.\\\",\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.downstream_study and study.* grounding sources are absent. Do not manufacture an original-incumbent comparison, search improvement, or scored/unscored attempt accounting from memory or aggregate campaign totals.\\\",\n+    \\\"The bibliography is present but central PPI/PPI++, exact-binomial, and empirical-Bernstein sources are missing. Existing DML and GCV metadata are relevant leads, not proof of having read those works. Off-topic retrieval records do not enlarge the study's scientific scope.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Honest frozen-score controls\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The studied estimator fits clipped ridge affine/spline score transforms on complementary labeled folds, uses rho=N/(n+N), and returns a Wilson-style stabilized asymptotic Wald interval, with a sample-size-only exact-binomial branch below 16 labels. This is the evaluated primary method, not a universally finite-sample-valid procedure.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Evaluated PPI++ mean interval\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Primary efficiency comparator with paired endpoints and uncertainty in all seven conditions; identifies the single small width reduction and six width increases. Describe the evaluated comparator, not all possible PPI++ implementations.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Evaluated PPI mean interval\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Original prediction-powered reference has measured endpoints and reveals different width/coverage behavior from PPI++, especially in the rare-outcome condition. Include in the compact main results table and rare-outcome figure, with complete comparisons in the supplement.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Labeled-only asymptotic mean interval\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Separates benefits over label-only normal inference from benefits over prediction-powered inference; its rare-outcome collapse is measured rather than an untested failure hypothesis.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Labeled-only exact binomial interval\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Provides a finite-sample coverage reference under independent Bernoulli sampling. Its conservatism and width are essential context, not a matched-validity justification for the asymptotic primary method.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Bounded componentwise safety construction\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Source implements separate empirical-Bernstein residual/control bounds and fixed-weight aggregation. Explain assumptions and union-bound logic as a theoretical alternative, never as an evaluated series or a reason to label the returned interval exact.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Use final.evidence.episodes as the numerical source, especially episodes[0].solution.case_summaries and all episodes[*].solution.cases. Summary coverage, paired mean differences, and zero-width counts were checked against the 256 records for each case. Retain neutral labels C1-C7 because generators, named datasets, and case-specific sample sizes are not identified in these records.\\\",\n+    \\\"Primary paired comparison: candidate-minus-PPI++ mean width difference is -0.00030173260155952255 in C2, with reported 95% interval [-0.0004003584986521721, -0.000203106704466873]. The other six differences are positive. These are condition-specific width findings, not a multiplicity-adjusted universal conclusion or a causal spline ablation.\\\",\n+    \\\"Display per-condition empirical coverage with reported uncertainty alongside width differences. Candidate coverage ranges from 0.9296875 to 0.95703125, and all seven reported candidate coverage intervals include 0.95. Non-rejection is not evidence that nominal coverage has been established.\\\",\n+    \\\"C5 is explicitly the low-mean condition: recorded truth 0.006800000000000005. Evaluated PPI++ and labeled-only asymptotic coverage are 0.55078125, each with 115 zero-width intervals. Candidate coverage is 0.9296875 with no zero-width intervals; exact-binomial coverage is 0.99609375. The candidate-minus-exact width difference is -0.000046988429386779555 with interval [-0.00032065914173324357, 0.0002266822829596845], so this comparison is inconclusive on mean width.\\\",\n+    \\\"Explain the observed label-only width reductions in C1-C3 and the small widening relative to labeled-only asymptotic intervals in C4, C6, and C7. Put PPI, PPI++, both labeled-only references, and candidate on a single compact comparison table, split into readable blocks if necessary.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final aggregate coverage 0.9425223214285714 and mean width 0.12988779848794016 are descriptive summaries, not evidence of exact 95% validity. Do not calculate a binomial uncertainty interval by treating all seven within-seed conditions as independent repetitions.\\\",\n+    \\\"Do not lead with the aggregate width ratio 64175.10539621905. Near-zero and zero comparator widths make ratio summaries misleading; emphasize raw paired width differences, interval distributions, coverage, and collapse counts instead. Do not infer the evaluator's ratio regularization formula.\\\",\n+    \\\"No measured affine-versus-spline ablation, safety-track width, oracle attainment, named real-data result, or matched comparison to the original search incumbent exists in the supplied paper evidence. Do not fill these gaps with unscored methods or source-only functions.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"An early full-text-width conceptual overview shows immutable labels/scores, complementary-fold score calibration, residual correction, the evaluated asymptotic interval, and a visually separate unmeasured safety construction.\\\",\n+    \\\"A full-text-width four-panel comparison pairs empirical coverage with candidate-minus-baseline width differences for C1-C4 and C5-C7; show the nominal coverage line and zero-difference line, with pointwise uncertainty and fixed method colors.\\\",\n+    \\\"A full-text-width two-panel rare-outcome diagnostic presents empirical interval-width distributions and zero-width counts in C5, making collapsed intervals visible instead of rewarding them through ratios.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"frozen_score_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the estimand, immutable-input restriction, fold isolation, and distinction between evaluated primary and unmeasured safety intervals immediately legible.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"information_flow\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none_conceptual\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"evaluated_primary_vs_unmeasured_safety\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected ICLR article style is single-column with a 5.5-inch text width and 9-inch text height. Use all 5.5 inches for a shallow five-object diagram; a half-text-width placement would crowd the fold-isolation labels. Place on page 1 or 2, preferably page 2 near the problem definition.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 5,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Five grouped objects: immutable labeled/unlabeled score inputs; complementary-fold fit/evaluate pairing; finite-N residual correction for E[Y]; evaluated stabilized asymptotic interval with size-only exact fallback; separate unmeasured bounded safety interval. Use solid primary and dashed safety connectors. No extra labels, predictor retraining, chronological arrows, or empirical-gain badge.\\\",\n+      \\\"target_size_inches\\\": [5.5, 1.8],\n+      \\\"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"intended_paper_footprint\\\": \\\"About one quarter page including caption, inside the formulation allocation.\\\",\n+      \\\"export_contract\\\": \\\"Retain editable draw.io source and prompt log; export vector PDF when available plus PNG at 300 DPI. Use PDF in LaTeX whenever present. If genuinely raster-only, regenerate at least 2400 pixels wide rather than upscaling.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"coverage_width_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Show that the small isolated PPI++ width gain and other width increases must be assessed jointly with empirical coverage and its uncertainty.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"paired_forest_composite\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"evaluation_condition\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"empirical_coverage_and_paired_mean_width_difference\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"C1-C4_then_C5-C7_with_coverage_and_width_columns\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Use a 5.5-inch-wide, 2-by-2 grid in the inspected single-column style: coverage left, width difference right, C1-C4 above C5-C7. This keeps at most four conditions in any panel without shrinking seven long case labels or five method series into half a text column. Subpanels are approximately 2.4 inches wide and use concise labels and shared legends.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Coverage panels: candidate, evaluated PPI++, labeled-only asymptotic, and exact binomial, with the reported 95% coverage intervals and a 0.95 reference. Width panels: paired candidate-minus-PPI++, candidate-minus-labeled-asymptotic, and candidate-minus-exact differences with reported 95% intervals and a zero line. Negative means narrower, not necessarily valid or superior. Preserve all seven conditions in fixed numeric order; group them only to satisfy readability. Width panels may use separately labeled linear scales because C5's difference is much larger. State pointwise rather than simultaneous uncertainty. PPI comparisons remain in the table and rare-outcome figure.\\\",\n+      \\\"target_size_inches\\\": [5.5, 4.3],\n+      \\\"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 8.5,\n+      \\\"intended_paper_footprint\\\": \\\"About three fifths of a page including caption, inside the main comparison allocation.\\\",\n+      \\\"export_contract\\\": \\\"Generate both PDF and PNG from plotting source, with PNG at 300 DPI; reference the PDF from LaTeX. Never recover legibility by raster upscaling.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"rare_outcome_diagnostic\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Expose degenerate comparator intervals and the inconclusive width comparison with exact-binomial inference in the observed low-mean condition.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"ecdf_and_zero_width_counts\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"interval_method\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"interval_width_distribution_and_zero_width_count\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"C5_only\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Two side-by-side quantitative panels need the complete 5.5-inch single-column text width for readable ECDF axes, zero-width annotations, and four method labels. A half-width figure would make each panel too narrow. Use a shared four-method legend and label counts rather than a thresholded success metric.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Use candidate, evaluated PPI++, evaluated PPI, and exact binomial. Plot empirical width CDFs from the 256 C5 endpoint records, retaining the mass at zero on a linear axis; show the corresponding zero-width counts in panel two. Mention that the labeled-only asymptotic comparator also has 115 zero-width intervals in the caption and main table. Pair the figure with coverage values and intervals in the main text, not only in the supplement. Do not claim the zero-width diagnostic proves the internal cause of every miss.\\\",\n+      \\\"target_size_inches\\\": [5.5, 2.2],\n+      \\\"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 8.5,\n+      \\\"intended_paper_footprint\\\": \\\"About one third page including caption, inside the failure-analysis allocation.\\\",\n+      \\\"export_contract\\\": \\\"Generate PDF and 300-DPI PNG from the same plotting source and reference the PDF. Any unavoidable raster-only full-width replacement must be regenerated at least 2400 pixels wide.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Provide the source-level implementation detail, complete measured comparator evidence, and reproducibility boundaries needed to audit the standalone claim without moving its isolated gain, widening, low-mean failures, or coverage caveats out of the main paper.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete paired interval comparisons\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tables for all seven conditions and all measured baseline intervals: empirical coverage and its reported limits, paired mean width differences and limits, recorded ratio diagnostics clearly distinguished from ratio-of-means, and zero-width counts. Derive tabulations only from final episode records; mark any derived summary and record its formula. Do not copy the first episode's aggregate case summaries 256 times.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Calibration and interval implementation\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Source-grounded pseudocode for fold generation, training-only quantile knots, ridge/GCV selection, clipping, rho weighting, pooled variance approximation, boundary stabilization, and the size-only exact fallback. Describe affine-only and safety functions as available but unmeasured. Cite result.top_program_01 as the path link, not as numerical evidence of these implementation properties; use the linked program.py and METHOD.md directly.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Fixed-control variance and separate safety argument\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Check the source's fixed-control variance decomposition, conditional-mean oracle expression, and affine projection gap under iid common-population sampling and an independently frozen predictor. Extend with the componentwise empirical-Bernstein union-bound argument under bounded residuals and controls, explaining cross-fold dependence and fixed nonnegative weights. Label these as mathematical arguments, not measured oracle attainment or a guarantee for the returned asymptotic interval.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Evidence extraction and reproducibility boundaries\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document final evidence paths and hashes, the 256 episode seeds, case identifiers, recorded truths, paired endpoint extraction, and scripts mapping every proposed table/plot to records. Preserve the final qualification and the unverified diagnostic-trust annotation. Explain that the supplied study helpers are not an executed end-to-end experiment runner, and that case generators, case-specific n/N values, and a separately staged final source tree are not recoverable here; reproducing figures from records is narrower than reproducing data generation.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\", \\\"result.top_program_01\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the documented agent-assisted ideation, candidate preparation, reference planning, and paper framing/writing roles using the visible task and source-preparation records; distinguish automated evaluation from author-generated numerical evidence. Do not invent model identifiers, manual verification, or unlogged human contributions. Final episode records provide the provenance anchor for measured results, not a claim that LLMs verified statistical validity.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Phases\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Valid Result\\\",\n+    \\\"Iteration History\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Winning Program\\\",\n+    \\\"Universal Improvements\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"uniformly narrower valid intervals\\\",\n+    \\\"95% coverage is established because it was not rejected\\\",\n+    \\\"cross-fitting guarantees finite-sample validity\\\",\n+    \\\"the spline component caused the gain\\\",\n+    \\\"unscored attempts were measured losses\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"Scope: this is a standalone empirical/methodological limitations study, not a search diary, architecture contribution, or new universally valid CI procedure. Neutral cases are separate evidence blocks under one common binary-mean question; do not name a dataset from the task's optional menu or infer case mechanisms from observed gains.\\\",\n+    \\\"Qualification audit, private provenance: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, final.qualification.correct=true. No failed final qualification is reported in this run. Do not overwrite these with search flags or imply that qualification proves scientific validity. Gate-specific diagnostics beyond the supplied fields are unknown. If later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, preserve that outcome and limitations in the paper, review, audit, and revisions without guessing whether the cause is performance, validity, or adaptivity.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private provenance only: use result.top_program_01 to locate the selected source. With no downstream_study or study.* sources, omit search-score deltas, scored/unscored attempt counts, and original-incumbent superiority claims. Internal pipeline labels and source paths belong in private grounding or anonymized reproducibility records, not reader-facing titles or claims.\\\",\n+    \\\"Target discipline: E[Y] is the binary superpopulation mean. Inputs are fixed across methods within a repetition; uncertainty is assessed over repeated draws, not by silently changing the target to the realized finite-pool mean. Common-population iid sampling and predictor independence are assumptions, not properties established for unidentified generators. The finite-N oracle formulas and fold-variance approximation must be distinguished.\\\",\n+    \\\"Theory can explain the opportunity, not attribute the measured effect: for a fixed control, state the variance decomposition and conditional-mean optimum under explicit assumptions; the estimated clipped spline family need not attain the oracle. Include no nonlinear-versus-affine efficacy claim without measured matched ablation. Treat the safety construction as separate and unmeasured throughout captions, abstract, review, and conclusions.\\\",\n+    \\\"Uncertainty: retain the supplied per-condition coverage intervals and paired width-difference intervals, label them pointwise, and state that seven conditions and multiple baselines were examined. Existing non-rejection flags are not equivalence tests or guarantees. Describe seeds as seeded repetitions; independence of all within-seed conditions is not established. Endpoint replay flags and unverified candidate diagnostics do not certify statistical coverage.\\\",\n+    \\\"Venue/layout: read VENUE.md and the inspected templates/iclr/paper.tex plus paper.sty; the practical geometry is one 5.5-inch text column by 9 inches. All three required figures use the full text width, not a nonexistent two-column figure* geometry. Target readable final labels of at least 8.5 points for plots and 9 points for the overview. Keep diagrams shallow and use a 2-by-2 grid rather than seven-category crowded panels.\\\",\n+    \\\"Body budget: target 8.5 pages excluding references: abstract/introduction and concrete contributions 1.25; formulation/related work plus early overview 1.25; method and limited theoretical analysis 2.0; evaluation design and provenance limits 1.0; direct coverage/width comparison including compact table 1.75; rare-outcome analysis 0.75; limitations/conclusion 0.5. These allocations sum to 8.5 and include figures. Use available space for estimand clarity, fold isolation, comparator coverage, and failure analysis rather than more unsupported experiments. Final body must be 8-9 pages; if exactly 8 pages, the last must be at least 75% occupied. This is a plan, not a measured pagination result.\\\",\n+    \\\"Suggested thesis-first sections: Introduction; Problem and Related Work; Honest Frozen-Score Controls; Evaluation Design; Coverage and Width Across Conditions; Rare-Outcome Limits; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Explain the missing nonlinear ablation, absent safety measurement, unidentified generators/sample sizes, narrow binary target, and no distribution-shift or new-domain validation explicitly. No padding or chronological branch descriptions.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main evidence table: include all five evaluated inferential methods; omit the [0,1] sanity interval from headline efficiency comparisons. Use compact condition labels and split coverage/width blocks if needed. Keep the one C2 improvement, six PPI++ widenings, C5 collapse counts, and candidate coverage caveat in the main body. Do not infer evaluator internals from field names such as valid_gain_supported.\\\",\n+    \\\"Supplement: after the references use clearpage, appendix, and a substantive Supplementary Information section with the planned subsections. Route later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses there without changing this strategy. Keep evidence essential to the central thesis in the main text. Include the separate LLM Usage disclosure required by the venue.\\\",\n+    \\\"Template repair for later drafting: the staged ICLR scaffold contains a named author and iclrfinalcopy, so use anonymous review mode and remove author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, and identifying links. Preserve any orchestrator-owned watermark block. The staged style provides practical geometry but does not itself establish official ICLR 2026 template provenance; verify the required venue version through permitted official material before final submission.\\\",\n+    \\\"Literature limitation: references.bib/references_provenance.json presently supply DML and GCV metadata but omit the central permitted PPI/PPI++ starter works and exact-binomial/empirical-Bernstein foundations. Before a final manuscript, obtain and actually consult exact allowlisted starter/foundational sources; verify bibliographic metadata, including GCV's venue field. Do not invent missing citation keys or cite unrelated retrieval hits as padding. Never search citation networks, guess the prohibited paper, or inspect ambiguous follow-up material. This strategy stage performs no literature retrieval and makes no claim that metadata equals source consultation.\\\",\n+    \\\"Vector-first delivery: quantitative plotting scripts must emit PDF and PNG at 300 DPI, and LaTeX must reference PDF whenever available. Preserve editable concept-figure output and follow the orchestrator's generate-concept-figure handoff later, not during strategy generation. Raster-only replacements require regeneration at least 2400 pixels wide full-width or 1200 pixels wide column-width; never upscale. Keep method colors and validity labels consistent across figures.\\\",\n+    \\\"Evidence gaps are limitations, not promised experiments. Available endpoints suffice for the planned comparisons and CDFs; no new data collection, predictor retraining, safety-track rerun, or later ablation is necessary to make the narrow thesis readable. Do not report these missing studies as completed. Reproduction of the sealed data-generating experiment remains incomplete even if every table can be regenerated from the released records.\\\",\n+    \\\"Planning stage only: write neither paper.tex nor claims_grounding.json, generate no figures, and do not run final-paper validation. Validate only this strategy's JSON structure, source references, consistency, and output boundaries.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Strategy: Frozen-Score Mean Inference\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Status:** ready. **Family:** \"'`paper_standalone`, compatible with `write-paper-standalone`.\n+\n+**Provisional title:** *Frozen-Score Mean Inference: Width Gains and Coverage Limits*.\n+\n+**Central question:** With labels, unlabeled scores, and the predictor fixed within each comparison, what interval-width gains and coverage limitations does honest score calibration exhibit for a binary population mean relative to prediction-powered and labeled-only intervals?\n+\n+**Central thesis:** Across seven evaluated binary-mean conditions, honest score calibration has a small paired width advantage over the evaluated PPI++ comparator in only one condition; rare-outcome interval collapse shows why widths need coverage uncertainty and an exact-binomial reference alongside them.\n+\n+This is a standalone empirical/methodological limitations paper, not a claim of universal improvement or a demonstration that nonlinear calibration caused the observed gain. The shared object is binary superpopulation-mean inference from immutable inputs. Present neutral conditions C1-C7 as evidence blocks under that question, not as named application studies or chronological experiments.\n+\n+## Evidence and Qualification\n+\n+Read `paper_data.json.final_evaluation` independently. It reports a completed, qualified final evaluation. The authoritative qualification anchors are `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, and `final.qualification.correct`; no failed final qualification is reported here. This status is not a guarantee of nominal statistical coverage. Missing gate-specific diagnostics remain unknown, and neither replay flags nor unverified candidate diagnostics prove statistical validity. If later authoritative evidence changes qualification, preserve the reported outcome and limitations through writing, review, audit, and revision without guessing the cause.\n+\n+The numerical anchor is `final.evidence.episodes`: 256 seeded repetitions, each containing seven conditions and paired candidate/baseline intervals. The aggregate case summaries occur only at `episodes[0].solution.case_summaries`; individual records are under `episodes[*].solution.cases`. All seven coverage summaries, paired mean width differences, and baseline zero-width counts were checked against those records. The diagnostic-trust annotation is `unverified`; the plan relies on recorded endpoints, truths, and comparisons, not on candidate-supplied validity assertions.\n+\n+The final aggregate coverage is **0.9425223214285714** and mean width **0.12988779848794016** (`final.metric.coverage`, `final.metric.mean_width`). These are descriptive, not proof of 95% validity. Do not treat all seven within-seed cases as independent when constructing aggregate uncertainty. Per-condition candidate coverage ranges from **0.9296875** to **0.95703125**; every reported candidate coverage interval includes 0.95. Non-rejection is not equivalence or validation of nominal coverage.\n+\n+`downstream_study` and `study.*` grounding sources are absent. Omit search-score deltas, scored/unscored attempt accounting, and superiority to an original search incumbent. Missing evaluations are not measured losses. The measured PPI++ comparator is not automatically the original search incumbent. Internal selection metadata is private provenance, not a visible paper result.\n+\n+## Framing Alternatives and Edit Decision\n+\n+No resolved edit-context files, `previous_paper/`, `aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` are staged. This is fresh framing, not an update to a prior manuscript. The JSON enum is **recentered** only to describe recentering the broad task opportunity around the actual final evidence; it does not assert a prior paper existed.\n+\n+- **Preserve a generic improvement story:** reject. Only one condition is narrower than evaluated PPI++; finite-sample validity of the returned method is not established.\n+- **Broaden to a shared family of searched methods:** reject. Other branches do not supply the necessary measured comparisons; source-only functions and unsuccessful executions are not performance evidence.\n+- **Center the evaluated score-control method'\"'s width/coverage limits:** select. It has repeated paired measurements, uncertainty, a small isolated gain, widespread modest costs, and an informative low-mean failure comparison.\n+\n+The selected candidate source is under \"'`results/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/`, linked by `result.top_program_01`. Inspect `program.py`, `METHOD.md`, and `study.py` directly for implementation facts. The final evidence records a frozen program-tree digest, but a separate final source tree is not staged for file-by-file comparison. The candidate'\"'s preparation notes predate execution; final episode records supersede their absence-of-results statements, not their warnings about asymptotic versus safety intervals.\n+\n+## Method Groups\n+\n+1. **Honest frozen-score controls — proposed.** Two-fold complementary-label calibration; ridge affine and small piecewise-linear spline candidates selected by training-only GCV; clipped controls; finite-unlabeled-sample factor \"'`rho=N/(n+N)`; residual correction. The evaluated output is a Wilson-style stabilized asymptotic Wald interval, with a size-only Clopper-Pearson branch for fewer than 16 labels. Do not call the general procedure exact or an exact Wilson interval.\n+2. **Evaluated PPI++ mean interval — primary baseline.** The paired efficiency comparison is central. Restrict claims to this evaluated comparator rather than all implementations of the published method.\n+3. **Evaluated PPI mean interval — baseline.** Retain in the main table, rare-outcome plot, and complete supplement. Its behavior differs materially from PPI++.\n+4. **Labeled-only asymptotic mean interval — baseline.** Separates gains over label-only normal inference from gains over prediction-powered inference.\n+5. **Labeled-only exact binomial interval — baseline.** Finite-sample reference under iid Bernoulli sampling, not permission to transfer its guarantee to another estimator.\n+6. **Bounded componentwise safety construction — supporting theory only.** The source implements empirical-Bernstein component intervals and union-bound/fixed-weight aggregation separately. It was not the measured primary output; do not assign it empirical coverage or width.\n+\n+Exclude partition portfolios and likelihood branches from the main comparison. An affine-only matched calibration function exists but has no measured ablation in the supplied evidence. Likewise, the oracle frontier and safety helper are not executed evidence of superiority.\n+\n+Keep the target **E[Y]**, not the realized finite-pool mean. Inputs are fixed across methods within each repetition; frequentist uncertainty is over repeated draws. Common-population iid sampling and a predictor frozen independently of inference labels are assumptions, not established facts about unidentified generators. Explain the fixed-control variance decomposition, conditional-mean oracle, affine projection gap, and fold-variance approximation with their separate assumptions. A fixed clipped spline dictionary need not attain the oracle; cross-fitting does not make folds unconditionally independent.\n+\n+## Results That Carry the Story\n+\n+Use `final.evidence.episodes` for this entire section. Retain C1-C7 identifiers: the records do not identify datasets, generators, or case-specific sample sizes. Do not infer a nonlinear, shifted, or adversarial regime from a result pattern.\n+\n+- **One small PPI++ width gain:** in C2, candidate-minus-PPI++ mean width difference is **-0.00030173260155952255**, with reported 95% interval **[-0.0004003584986521721, -0.000203106704466873]**. The other six differences are positive. These are pointwise, condition-specific findings, not multiplicity-adjusted general improvement or evidence attributing the effect to splines.\n+- **Label-only context:** C1-C3 are narrower than labeled-only asymptotic inference; C4, C6, and C7 have small width increases against that baseline. Report the exact-binomial and PPI comparisons too, rather than selecting only favorable baselines.\n+- **Rare-outcome diagnostic:** C5 records truth **0.006800000000000005**. PPI++ and labeled-only asymptotic coverage are each **0.55078125**, with **115** zero-width intervals each. Candidate coverage is **0.9296875**, with no zero-width intervals; exact-binomial coverage is **0.99609375**. PPI has two zero-width intervals. Collapse and undercoverage are observable; the evaluator'\"'s internal cause for every miss is not identified.\n+- **Exact reference remains important:** in C5, candidate-minus-exact mean width difference is **-0.000046988429386779555**, with interval **[-0.00032065914173324357, 0.0002266822829596845]**. This width comparison is inconclusive. The candidate's absence of collapsed intervals does not establish nominal validity or superiority to exact inference.\n+- **Avoid unstable ratio headlines:** the retained aggregate width ratio is **64175.10539621905**. Zero and near-zero comparator widths make ratio summaries scientifically misleading; foreground paired differences and raw width distributions. Do not infer the evaluator's denominator regularization.\n+\n+The main table must include all five evaluated inferential methods. Split coverage and width blocks if necessary. Keep the C2 gain, six PPI++ widenings, C5 collapse counts, and candidate coverage caveat in the main body. The \"'`[0,1]` sanity interval is not a headline efficiency baseline. Do not translate evaluator flags into scientific validity claims.\n+\n+## Figures and Practical Geometry\n+\n+Inspected `paper.sty` and `.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex`. The style has **one 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height**. There is no two-column body: all required figures use full text width, not `figure*` to span nonexistent columns. The scaffold'\"'s author and final-copy mode must be replaced for anonymous review during later drafting. Practical geometry does not certify the official 2026 template version; verify that provenance before submission.\n+\n+### Figure 1 — \"'`frozen_score_overview`\n+\n+Required early conceptual diagram; generator **`generate-concept-figure`**. Place on page 1 or 2, preferably page 2 beside the problem definition. Target **5.5 × 1.8 inches**, full text width, approximately one quarter page including caption. Five grouped objects show immutable inputs, complementary-fold fitting/evaluation, residual correction targeting E[Y], the evaluated stabilized primary interval, and a separate unmeasured safety construction. Use solid versus dashed connectors for evaluated versus theoretical paths, not chronological discovery arrows. No predictor retraining or empirical-gain badge.\n+\n+Readability budget: **one panel, one panel per row, at most five object groups, three semantic series, labels at least 9 points**. Half-width would crowd fold isolation and track distinctions. Grounding: `result.top_program_01` for the source path, `final.evidence.episodes` for which primary output was measured. Retain editable draw.io output and prompt log; no figure generation occurs in this stage.\n+\n+### Figure 2 — `coverage_width_comparison`\n+\n+Required matplotlib composite; target **5.5 × 4.3 inches**, full text width, approximately three fifths page including caption. Use a **2 × 2 grid**: coverage left, paired width differences right; C1-C4 in the upper row, C5-C7 below. Keep fixed case order, not performance ranking. Each panel has at most four conditions, so seven cases do not crowd one axis.\n+\n+Coverage series: candidate, evaluated PPI++, labeled-only asymptotic, exact binomial. Show the reported coverage uncertainty and 0.95 reference. Difference series: candidate minus PPI++, labeled-only asymptotic, and exact; show reported uncertainty and zero reference. Negative means narrower, not automatically valid. PPI remains in the main table and rare-case figure. Clearly labeled different linear scales are permissible across width panels because C5 is much larger.\n+\n+Readability budget: **four panels, two per row, four categories per panel, four series maximum; final labels at least 8.5 points**. Approximately 2.4-inch subpanels, concise case labels, and shared legends make this possible without shrinking. Grounding: `final.evidence.episodes`, particularly the single attached set of case summaries. Explain that the uncertainty is pointwise, not simultaneous.\n+\n+### Figure 3 — `rare_outcome_diagnostic`\n+\n+Required matplotlib diagnostic; target **5.5 × 2.2 inches**, full text width, approximately one third page including caption. Two side-by-side panels show C5 empirical interval-width CDFs and zero-width counts for candidate, evaluated PPI++, evaluated PPI, and exact binomial. Retain the mass at zero on a linear width axis. Mention the labeled-only asymptotic baseline'\"'s matching 115 collapses in the caption and main table. Put coverage and its uncertainty in adjacent main text, not only the supplement.\n+\n+Readability budget: **two panels, two per row, four method categories, four series; final labels at least 8.5 points**. Full width gives each panel enough room for axes and method labels. Grounding: all 256 C5 endpoint records in \"'`final.evidence.episodes`. Do not imply the collapse diagnostic establishes the internal cause of every coverage miss.\n+\n+### Export Contract\n+\n+Quantitative plotting source emits **PDF and 300-DPI PNG**, and LaTeX references the PDF whenever available. Preserve editable concept output and export PDF when possible. For truly raster-only figures, regenerate at **at least 2400 pixels wide full-width or 1200 pixels wide column-width**; never upscale an existing raster. Use consistent method colors and validity labels. Exactly one overview uses `generate-concept-figure`; follow its later orchestration handoff rather than rendering it during strategy generation.\n+\n+## Body Budget and Organization\n+\n+Target **8.5 pages excluding references**, with figure footprints included:\n+\n+| Scientific content | Planned pages |\n+| --- | ---: |\n+| Abstract, introduction, concrete contributions | 1.25 |\n+| Problem and related work, including early overview | 1.25 |\n+| Honest controls and limited theoretical analysis | 2.00 |\n+| Evaluation design and provenance limitations | 1.00 |\n+| Direct coverage/width comparison and compact table | 1.75 |\n+| Rare-outcome analysis | 0.75 |\n+| Limitations and conclusion | 0.50 |\n+\n+Suggested thesis-first headings: **Introduction; Problem and Related Work; Honest Frozen-Score Controls; Evaluation Design; Coverage and Width Across Conditions; Rare-Outcome Limits; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion**. Additional space buys precise estimands, fold isolation, calibration/stabilization detail, comparator uncertainty, and a checked variance argument—not new experiments or a history of discarded approaches.\n+\n+The venue requires 8-9 body pages; if exactly eight pages, the final page must be at least 75% occupied. These are planned allocations, not a claim that pagination has been validated. Do not pad to meet them. Explicitly retain missing nonlinear ablation, unmeasured safety intervals, unidentified generators/sample sizes, narrow binary scope, no distribution-shift validation, and incomplete end-to-end reproduction.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information\n+\n+After references use a page break, appendix mode, and **Supplementary Information**. Its purpose is audit depth and substantive methods, not hiding central limitations. The following mirrored JSON entries are grounded in existing artifacts:\n+\n+1. **Complete paired interval comparisons** (`final.evidence.episodes`). All seven conditions and all recorded comparators, coverage limits, paired width differences and limits, ratio diagnostics distinguished from ratio-of-means, and zero-width counts. Document formulas for derived tables. Never duplicate the first episode'\"'s aggregate summaries across repetitions.\n+2. **Calibration and interval implementation** (\"'`result.top_program_01`, a path anchor). Use the linked `program.py` and `METHOD.md` for fold generation, train-only knots, ridge/GCV, clipping, rho weighting, approximate variance, stabilization, and the size-only exact fallback. Affine-only and safety functions are available but unmeasured; the scalar selection score does not substantiate implementation properties.\n+3. **Fixed-control variance and separate safety argument** (`result.top_program_01`, linked method sources). Check the decomposition, conditional-mean oracle, and affine projection gap under explicit assumptions. Explain componentwise bounded concentration, union bounds, fold dependence, and nonnegative endpoint weights. This is not observed oracle attainment or validity of the returned asymptotic interval.\n+4. **Evidence extraction and reproducibility boundaries** (`final.evidence.episodes`, `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.correct`, `result.top_program_01`). Record hashes, seeds, truths, endpoint extraction, and table/figure scripts. Retain qualification and diagnostic-trust annotations. Recreating figures from records is possible; case generators, case-specific n/N values, and a separately staged final source tree are not recoverable here. Study helpers are not an executed complete experiment runner.\n+5. **LLM Usage** (`result.top_program_01`, `final.evidence.episodes`, with role descriptions from visible task/source-preparation records). Disclose agent-assisted ideation, implementation preparation, reference planning, and framing/writing accurately; distinguish those roles from automated evaluation. Do not invent model identifiers, human checks, or claims of LLM-verified coverage.\n+\n+Later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses go here without retroactively altering this plan. Never move the isolated gain, widening, rare-outcome failures, or nominal-coverage caveat out of the main paper.\n+\n+## Literature, Anonymity, and Handoff\n+\n+`references.bib` and `references_provenance.json` exist, but central permitted PPI/PPI++ starter sources and exact-binomial/empirical-Bernstein foundations are missing. DML and GCV metadata are relevant leads, not proof of source consultation; GCV'\"'s venue field needs checking. Before final writing, consult exact allowlisted starter/foundational works and verify citation metadata. Do not invent keys or pad related work with off-topic retrieval hits. Do not guess or search for the prohibited paper, traverse citation networks, or inspect ambiguous follow-up material. This framing stage performs no retrieval and does not claim that metadata is reading.\n+\n+The venue is **ICLR 2026, anonymous conference review**. Remove names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, identifying links, and final-copy mode from the seeded scaffold later; preserve the orchestrator-owned watermark block. Include the separate LLM Usage disclosure. Do not falsely certify the old-looking staged style as the official current venue release.\n+\n+This stage writes no \"'`paper.tex`, no `claims_grounding.json`, and no figures, and runs no final-paper validation. Check only strategy structure, source references, consistency, and stage boundaries. Missing experiments remain missing, not promises converted into completed work.\n+\n+## Diary and Overclaim Guardrails\n+\n+Forbid headings centered on **Search Progression, Campaign Phases, Milestones, First Valid Result, Iteration History, Experiment A / Experiment B, Winning Program, Universal Improvements**.\n+\n+Forbid visible phrases **we then tried; subsequent improvements; next-best; later variants; first valid result; correctness rate; correct and eligible; eligible; combined_score; rubric; worker_01; worker_02; uniformly narrower valid intervals; 95% coverage is established because it was not rejected; cross-fitting guarantees finite-sample validity; the spline component caused the gain; unscored attempts were measured losses; state of the art**. Internal selection identifiers in this memo are private provenance only, never recommended reader-facing language.\n+\n+The framing wins because it uses the strongest paired final evidence, preserves unfavorable comparisons, and identifies a useful limitation without inventing a mechanism, a dataset, a universal winner, or an exact guarantee. No failure reason applies to this bounded strategy; bibliography and reproduction gaps remain explicit final-manuscript limitations or remediation requirements.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
